     sskkeeyyaauuddiitt — warn users if their S/Key will soon expire

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     sskkeeyyaauuddiitt [--aaii] [--ll _l_i_m_i_t]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     sskkeeyyaauuddiitt searches through the files in _/_e_t_c_/_s_k_e_y for users whose S/Key
     sequence number is less than _l_i_m_i_t, and mails them a reminder to run
     skeyinit(1) soon.

     The options are as follows:

     --aa      Check all keys in _/_e_t_c_/_s_k_e_y.  This option is only available to
             the superuser and is useful to run regularly via cron(8).

     --ii      Interactive mode.  Don't send mail, just print to the standard
             output.

     --ll _l_i_m_i_t
             The limit used to determine whether or not a user should be noti‐
             fied.  The default is to notify if there are fewer than 12 keys
             left.

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/skey  directory containing user entries for S/Key

